Files derived from OPSIN
------------------------
OPSIN is MIT licensed (Copyright (c) Daniel Lowe and contributors; source:
https://github.com/dan2097/opsin). These files of this repository hold data
taken from OPSIN's resource files (uk/ac/cam/ch/wwmm/opsin/resources/ in the
OPSIN jar and source tree); each .py file carries the notice in its header.

- src/orthonym/data/opsin_imports/regex_tokens_xml.json holds OPSIN 2.9.0's
  resource regexTokens.xml, byte-identical to the entry in the jar above
  (SHA-256 recorded in the file). It lets the name-grammar check load without
  the jar.
- src/orthonym/data/opsin_imports/*.py, generated by
  scripts/import_opsin_xml.py from OPSIN's XML resources:
    amino_acids_opsin.py          aminoAcids.xml
    aryl_groups.py                arylGroups.xml
    carbohydrates_opsin.py        carbohydrates.xml, carbohydrateSuffixes.xml
    carboxylic_acids_opsin.py     carboxylicAcids.xml
    cyclic_groups.py              simpleCyclicGroups.xml,
                                  cyclicUnsaturableHydrocarbon.xml
    functional_terms.py           functionalTerms.xml
    fusion_components_opsin.py    fusionComponents.xml
    natural_products_opsin.py     naturalProducts.xml
    simple_groups.py              simpleGroups.xml
    substituent_names_opsin.py    simpleSubstituents.xml, substituents.xml
    suffix_rules.py               suffixRules.xml, suffixApplicability.xml
    word_rules.py                 wordRules.xml
    __init__.py                   merges the modules above
- src/orthonym/data/hw_stems.py (from hwSuffixes.xml) and the OPSIN amino-acid
  entries of src/orthonym/data/amino_acids.py (from aminoAcids.xml).


Fonts in the README pictures
----------------------------
The README pictures that carry text (assets/readme-*.svg) embed two fonts as
WOFF2 data (an SVG loaded as an image cannot fetch a font). The WOFF2 files they are built from, by
docs/readme/build.py, are in docs/readme/src/fonts/.

- Public Sans 2.001 (regular, semibold and italic faces): SIL Open Font License,
  Version 1.1; Copyright 2015 The Public Sans Project Authors.
  Source: https://github.com/uswds/public-sans
- JetBrains Mono 2.211: SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1; Copyright 2020 The
  JetBrains Mono Project Authors. Source: https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono
- docs/readme/src/fonts/ also holds Saira Condensed 0.072 (not embedded in any
  picture): SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1; Copyright 2016 The Saira
  Project Authors, reserved font name "Saira".
  Source: https://github.com/Omnibus-Type/Saira

The licence text, as the font files cite it: https://scripts.sil.org/OFL.

RDKit and the other Python dependencies are installed by pip under their own
licences and are not redistributed by this repository.
